# win32u/freetype: Fix tmExternalLeading for CFF fonts.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/10603 state=opened
# This fixes font scaling issues with CFF fonts this was discovered from games utilizing DxLib.

https://github.com/yumetodo/DxLib/tree/master

https://dxlib.xsrv.jp/index.html

I've ran tests on Windows and to confirm that this change is consistent with a number of fonts.

Before:

![image.png](/uploads/a398d5543df8561f1a6fbe9edded3b45/image.png){width="801" height="600"}

After (this matches the windows visual from testing in a VM):

![image.png](/uploads/cf4e4c8753b3482dd24211b519a5fe23/image.png){width="767" height="572"}

Related Proton Issue:

https://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7299

Full Disclosure:

An LLM was used to assist in finding this bug, the original fix written by the LLM wrote a loader binary that changed the pointers for `GetTextMetricsA` and `GetTextMetricsW` to point to a custom implementation that always set `tmExternalLeading`. The LLM determined that `GDI returns 0 when (winAscent + winDescent) > (Ascender - Descender)`, after testing on WIndows I found this to be incorrect, the actual difference is that CFF fonts always set `tmExternalLeading` to 0.
